<title>USA: AMEX begins trading LEAPS on Republic.</title>
<headline>AMEX begins trading LEAPS on Republic.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The American Stock Exchange (AMEX) said it would trade long term equity anticipation securities (LEAPS) on shares of Republic Industries Inc beginning Friday.</p>
<p>The exchange said the LEAPS would have strike prices of 20, 25 and 30, with an expiration in January 1999. LETCO-Specialist LP is the specialist.</p>
<p>Equity LEAPS traded in units of 100 shares of stock per contract, are American-style and settle in stock.</p>
<p>((--Derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
